  book_summary: A little girl, beloved by everyone and especially by her grandmother, receives a red velvet cap and is called Little Red Riding Hood. Her mother sends her through the woods with cake and wine for her sick grandmother. On the way she meets the wolf. Later, the wolf goes to the grandmother’s house, pretends to be Red Riding Hood, tricks the grandmother, and swallows her whole. The narrative then returns to the beginning of the story, telling how the girl got her red cap and was sent by her mother, and closes by repeating the wolf’s arrival at the grandmother’s house and the grandmother’s death.


